From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Rogers <pdr@chromium.org>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:35:38 -0700
Subject: [html-in-canvas] Fix filter dirty bit clearing

This patch moves clearing of `filter_on_effect_node_dirty_` and
`backdrop_filter_on_effect_node_dirty_` out of `PaintLayer`'s filter
builder methods (which are now `const`) and into
`PaintLayer::ClearFilterAndBackdropFilterOnEffectNodeDirty()`, called
from `PaintPropertyTreeBuilder::UpdateForSelf` once the object's last
fragment updates.

Previously, `UpdateCompositorFilterOperationsForFilter` and
`UpdateCompositorFilterOperationsForBackdropFilter` cleared the shared
`PaintLayer` dirty bits immediately. An earlier fragment in a multicol
container would clear the dirty bit before later fragments updated,
causing those fragments to early-return and keep stale filter
operations after moving into a `<canvas content=drawable>` subtree.

Fixed: 574759287
Change-Id: I9efea4ec9e717e2d087376ab21b925313bc93a71
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8639479
Commit-Queue: Philip Rogers <pdr@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kent Tamura <tkent@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1726725}
Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
paint_layer.cc: UpdateCompositorFilterOperationsForBackdropFilter() keeps
this branch's StyleRef() accessor; the const-qualification and the
removal of the dirty-bit clears are as upstream.

